@@ -8750,6 +8750,16 @@ static void UI_RunCinematicFrame(int handle)
  * skipped that step got a working mod with a dead status key and no way to
  * tell the difference from a broken one.
  *
+ * One of these is not narration at all. `weapalt` is how a rifle goes to
+ * its scope, a mortar and an MG are set down, and a satchel is detonated,
+ * and the stock config binds it to MOUSE2 and to nothing else - it is the
+ * only action in default.cfg with no key. Played from the keyboard alone
+ * the scope is therefore unreachable, which is the same defect as the
+ * limbo panel being mouse-only, and it cost a tester a session of trying
+ * to scope an FG 42 and hearing nothing because they never got into the
+ * scope. KP_SLASH is free in default.cfg *and* in default_left.cfg, which
+ * F9 and F10 are not.
+ *
  * F5, F6 and F8 are free in the engine's own default.cfg - it binds F1-F4,
  * F7 and F11-F12 and leaves these three alone - so claiming them takes
  * nothing away from a default install.
@@ -8776,11 +8786,14 @@ static void UI_AccessibilityInstallBinds(void)
 		const char *replaces;
 	} binds[] =
 	{
